WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.933
Arc Business Operating Account asks whether a business can fund its next order
without spending cash already promised elsewhere.

00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:13.779
We built and checked the contract, app, and accounting in this Arc Studio
workspace.

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:17.537
Codex assisted with review, browser operation, and verified exports.

00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:23.800
This is a controlled demonstration using real USDC on Arc mainnet, with
fictional, owner-controlled businesses.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.683
This review was captured before the owner signed.

00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:30.206
Three buyers commit one hundred goods units.

00:00:30.206 --> 00:00:35.973
Their own cash and prefunded credit pay zero point zero nine USDC to the
approved supplier.

00:00:35.973 --> 00:00:39.938
The close records zero point zero four five USDC of principal.

00:00:39.938 --> 00:00:43.542
Each buyer keeps zero point zero one in protected cash.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:47.867
The wallet fee ceiling was zero point zero two eight eight USDC.

00:00:48.867 --> 00:00:52.063
The owner personally confirmed the transaction in MetaMask.

00:00:52.063 --> 00:01:01.252
The public explorer shows a successful commit plan call on Business Kernel, at
block twenty-eight million, eight hundred forty-two thousand, nine hundred
fifty-two.

00:01:01.252 --> 00:01:08.045
This is the actual transaction from the public application, not a local
simulation or a testnet transaction.

00:01:09.045 --> 00:01:15.260
The receipt shows zero point zero nine USDC moving from the contract to the
approved supplier.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:21.863
The actual network fee was zero point zero one three eight five three two
three eight USDC.

00:01:21.863 --> 00:01:31.186
Thirty-five independent checks passed on the owner Mac and again in Arc
Studio, including the exact call, finality, payout, principal, protected cash,
and custody.

00:01:32.186 --> 00:01:35.292
Here is the live Cloudflare Workers app after settlement.

00:01:35.292 --> 00:01:36.673
The operation is committed.

00:01:36.673 --> 00:01:43.576
Cash and debt remain separate: buyer A retains zero point zero one USDC and
owes zero point zero one six.

00:01:43.576 --> 00:01:46.338
The kernel holds zero point zero three five.

00:01:46.338 --> 00:01:51.861
The same public app displays the confirmed transaction and the books produced
from its chain evidence.

00:01:52.861 --> 00:01:57.989
A page reload recovered the same hash and nonce as confirmed, with books
posted.

00:01:57.989 --> 00:02:04.582
The persistent ledger has one settlement event, twenty-eight balanced journal
lines, and one gas record for this close.

00:02:04.582 --> 00:02:06.047
Nineteen recovery checks passed.

00:02:06.047 --> 00:02:12.641
The shared accounting core runs on SQLite in Studio and on SQLite-backed
Durable Objects in the public Worker.

00:02:13.641 --> 00:02:18.490
The total zero point zero four five USDC principal remains outstanding.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:26.865
Physical delivery is not independently verified, and this is not a bank,
commercial credit service, or externally audited product.

00:02:26.865 --> 00:02:30.392
MetaMask displayed a malicious-site warning during the demonstration.

00:02:30.392 --> 00:02:35.682
The owner reviewed it personally; this transaction does not clear that
classification.

00:02:35.682 --> 00:02:41.413
The app, repository, original Studio project, contract, and receipt are linked
for review.
